# Test-Driven Development (TDD) Playbook

Follow this discipline to develop reliable features and bug fixes with automated test coverage.

## The Red-Green-Refactor Cycle

### 1. RED (Write a Failing Test)
- Focus on behavior and contracts, not internal implementation details.
- Write the smallest possible test case specifying the next unit of behavior.
- Run the test suite and verify that the test fails **for the expected reason**.

### 2. GREEN (Make It Pass)
- Write only the minimum amount of code required to make the test pass.
- Avoid building unrequested abstractions or premature optimizations.
- Verify that all tests pass cleanly.

### 3. REFACTOR (Clean & Optimize)
- Improve code readability, eliminate duplication, and enhance naming.
- Ensure contracts remain unchanged and all tests continue to pass.

## Quality Checklist
- Tests are fast, isolated, and deterministic (no network/time flakiness).
- Edge cases are covered: empty inputs, maximum boundaries, error triggers.
- Mocks are used sparingly—prefer real implementations or lightweight fakes.
